# Implementation Plan: OneMap Singapore API 3-Day Token Renewal & Supabase Edge Functions Setup

This plan details the server-side authentication, automatic 3-day token renewal (with a 6-hour buffer), concurrency protection, rate limiting, and Supabase Edge Functions proxy architecture for OneMap Singapore APIs.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Credential Security**:
> OneMap credentials (`ONEMAP_USERNAME` / `ONEMAP_EMAIL` & `ONEMAP_PASSWORD`) will ONLY reside in Supabase Edge Function secrets and server environment variables. Zero credentials, tokens, or auth headers will ever be exposed to or bundled inside the React Native / Expo app.

> [!NOTE]
> **Token Renewal Buffer & Concurrency**:
> * Token Expiration: ~3 days (~72 hours).
> * Renewal Safety Buffer: **6 hours** prior to expiration.
> * Concurrency Safety: Single in-flight Promise mutex locks concurrent requests while refreshing tokens, preventing duplicate authentication calls.

